# Cursor styles (web standards)

Match the [CSS `cursor` keywords](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/cursor) and platform defaults. The cursor should communicate **what will happen**, not merely that something is clickable.

Per the CSS UI / W3C definition: **`pointer` indicates a link** — not buttons or other controls.

| Interaction | Cursor | Use when |
|---|---|---|
| Link / navigation | `cursor-pointer` | `<a href>`, Next.js `<Link>`, or controls that navigate like a link |
| Button / control | default (omit) | `<button>`, tabs, switches, icon buttons, clear/dismiss, menus — keep the platform arrow |
| Text / selection | `cursor-text` | Inputs, textareas, selectable text regions |
| Copy | `cursor-copy` | Primary action is copy to clipboard (or drag-copy) |
| Not allowed | `cursor-not-allowed` | Disabled or blocked actions (`disabled:cursor-not-allowed`) |
| Grab / reorder | `cursor-grab` / `cursor-grabbing` | Draggable handles (grab → grabbing while dragging) |
| Move | `cursor-move` | Something can be moved without a grab metaphor |
| Resize | `cursor-ew-resize` / `cursor-ns-resize` / `cursor-col-resize` / `cursor-row-resize` | Resize edges and splitters |
| Busy (blocking) | `cursor-wait` | UI is blocked; user should wait |
| Busy (non-blocking) | `cursor-progress` | Work in progress but interaction still allowed |
| Help | `cursor-help` | Help or extra info is available on hover |
| Precise pick | `cursor-crosshair` | Pixel/region selection |
| Zoom | `cursor-zoom-in` / `cursor-zoom-out` | Zoom affordances |

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — pointer on a button (pointer means “link” in CSS)
<button type="button" onClick={handleClear} className="cursor-pointer ..." />

// ✅ GOOD — native button keeps the default arrow
<button type="button" onClick={handleClear} className="..." />

// ✅ GOOD — real navigation gets pointer
<Link href="/colors" className="cursor-pointer ...">Colors</Link>
<a href="https://example.com" className="cursor-pointer ...">Docs</a>

// ✅ GOOD — exception: a button styled and behaving as a text link
<button type="button" className="cursor-pointer underline text-fg-primary ...">
  View details
</button>

// ✅ GOOD — copy affordance
<button type="button" onClick={handleCopy} className="cursor-copy ..." />

// ✅ GOOD — disabled
<button type="button" disabled className="disabled:cursor-not-allowed ..." />
```

Rules of thumb:

- Prefer **semantic elements** (`<a>` / `<button>`) and let the UA default stand unless you need a specific keyword above.
- Do **not** add `cursor-pointer` to every clickable control. Reserve it for links and link-like navigation.
- If a `<button>` is visually and behaviorally a text link, `cursor-pointer` is OK so it matches link affordance.
- Don’t put interactive cursors on non-interactive wrappers (`div`/`span` with no activation behavior).
- Disabled: use `disabled:cursor-not-allowed` (and reduce hover affordance).
- Prefer `cursor-copy` when the primary action is copying — not `cursor-pointer`.
